 esophageal obstruction, or other conditions that necessitate long-term nutritional support. It is commonly used in various clinical scenarios, including for patients with chronic conditions, those requiring prolonged feeding, and even in premature newborns.\n\nThe gastrostomy procedure typically involves placing a tube through the abdominal wall directly into the stomach, allowing for enteral feeding. This method ensures that patients receive adequate nutrition when they cannot eat by mouth, making it a critical intervention in managing nutritional needs. The procedure may be part of a broader treatment plan for individuals with severe dysphagia or low weight, as it provides a reliable means of nutritional intake.\n\nIn summary, gastrostomía is a vital surgical intervention designed to support patients who require enteral nutrition, ensuring they receive the necessary sustenance for their health and well-being.", "EVALUACIÓN FUNCIONAL:Functional evaluation is a process used to assess the capabilities of patients with dysphagia, involving various clinical techniques.", "TRATAMIENTO ESPECÍFICO:Specific treatment refers to the tailored therapeutic approaches developed for patients with dysphagia based on their individual assessments.", "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO DE PONTEVEDRA (HUPA):HUPA is a hospital that collaborates with the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofaríngea to ensure the nutritional needs of patients are met through individualized dietary plans.", "EQUIPO DE NUTRICIÓN CLÍNICA Y DIETÉTICA (UNCYD):The UNCyD team is responsible for assessing and monitoring the nutritional status of patients, ensuring appropriate dietary interventions are implemented.", "TEST DE VOLUMEN-VISCOSIDAD:The volume-viscosity test is a clinical evaluation performed by nursing staff to assess the swallowing capabilities of patients.", "ENDOCINOLOGÍA:The Endocrinología (Endocrinology) service deals with hormonal and metabolic disorders, which can impact nutritional status and swallowing.", "CONSULTA PRIMERA DISFAGIA OROFARÍNGEA:The Consulta Primera Disfagia Orofaríngea is a specialized consultation for the initial assessment of patients suspected of having oropharyngeal dysphagia.", "VIDEOFLOUROSCOPIAS:Videofluoroscopias are diagnostic procedures performed to assess swallowing function in patients with dysphagia.", "MUST:The Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool (MUST) is a comprehensive screening tool designed to identify adults at risk of malnutrition. It is recommended by the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism (ESPEN) for use in community settings and various healthcare environments. MUST serves as a valuable resource for assessing nutritional risk in the general population, helping healthcare professionals to identify individuals who may be malnourished or at risk of malnutrition. This tool is particularly effective in screening patients and community members, facilitating early intervention and management of malnutrition. Overall, MUST is recognized as an essential instrument for evaluating nutritional status and addressing malnutrition risk among adults.", "MNA S-F:The Mini Nutritional Assessment Short-Form (MNA S-F) is a tool used to evaluate the nutritional status of elderly patients.", "ALIMENTOS SEGUROS:The safe foods provided by the Servicio de Cocina Hospitalaria for the evaluation of dysphagia include yogurt and custard."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}